<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikola I of Montenegro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1841–1921</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Nicholas I of Montenegro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikola I Petrović-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petar-ii-petrovic-njegos">Njegoš</a> ruled Montenegro as prince from 1860 and as king from 1910. Victories over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> won recognition of independence at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> in 1878 and new territory including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niksic">Nikšić</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podgorica">Podgorica</a> and Bar. He fought in the Balkan Wars and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, went into exile in 1916 and was deposed when Montenegro joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikola-i-of-montenegro.jpg" alt="Nikola I of Montenegro" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicholas_I_of_Montenegro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
